# Performance — WPNest

## Images

- Use `wp_get_attachment_image()` — never raw `<img>`.
- Set `loading="lazy"` by default; `eager` + `fetchpriority="high"` for hero images only.
- Use `sizes` and `srcset` via WordPress responsive image helpers.
- Use Tailwind classes for sizing: `class="w-full h-full object-cover"` — no inline styles.

## Queries

- Never use `query_posts()`.
- Set `no_found_rows => true` when not paginating.
- Cache expensive queries with `wp_cache_get()` / `wp_cache_set()`.
- Avoid `post__not_in` on large datasets.

## CSS & Tailwind

- Tailwind CSS v4 generates only the classes actually used via `@source` scanning — **no manual PurgeCSS needed**.
- Do not load additional global stylesheets. Add new styles as `@utility` in `sources/css/style.css` or as a new `@import`-ed CSS file.
- Use `hidden`, `block`, `lg:block`, `lg:hidden` for responsive show/hide — not separate stylesheets.
- Avoid long `@apply` chains in `@utility` if the same result can be achieved with a short class list in the HTML.

## JavaScript

- No render-blocking scripts (all theme scripts enqueued with `type="module"`).
- Bundle per-block JS — lazy-load with `import()` inside a DOM check.
- Don't load all scripts globally — only eager-load global UI (menu, navigation).
